    "updated_at": "2015-10-29T15:12:45Z",
    "body": "We can't use `metadata` for **new** kinds that we want to add to the spec. This is just making sure that the behavior in legacy UAs is sane when we extend the kinds we have. (Granted I don't expect this to happen often, if at all, but forward-compatible design is usually good anyway.)\n\nOK I misremembered how `metadata` tracks get enabled; I thought they were all set to `hidden` automatically, but you're right.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
